[[File:NarHida.png|thumb|right|250px|Nar Hida was a Luptoomian.]]
'''Luptoomians''' were a group that included the [[human]] [[Nar Hida]] who wore Luptoomian fashion while he was traveling in a [[Color|green]] spiked [[cloak]] on board the [[AA-9 Freighter-Liner]] ''[[Jendirian Valley]]''<ref name="BMF50">{{BuildFalconCite|50|Starship Fact File}}</ref> in [[22 BBY]].<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|II}} to [[22 BBY]].</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
A Luptoomian appeared in the [[2002]] [[prequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the group was identified in "AA-9 Coruscant Starfreighter," an article published in the "[[Starship Fact File]]" department of the magazine [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 50|''Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon'' 50]],<ref name="BMF50" /> which was written by [[Tim Veekhoven]]<ref name="Veekhoven">{{Twitter|sompeetalay|1036289998377680897|[[Tim Veekhoven]]|quote=#BuildtheMillenniumFalcon: "These officials, led by Constable Marcel Shradeer, received the authority to intervene whenever problems arose between the passengers." [Although not pictured, this was meant to be Shradeer. Issue 50: AA-9 Coruscant Freighter] @WookOfficial|archivedate=20210602073808}}</ref> and published around [[December 16]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BMFdates|50}}</ref>

The name originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where the [[Luptoomian/Legends|Luptoomian]]s were first identified by [[Gregory Walker]],<ref name="Walker">{{Blog|narbflick|9|Nar Hida: The Story Behind the Story}}</ref> under the username "NarbFlick," through the [[StarWars.com]] [[Hyperspace: The Official Star Wars Fan Club|Hyperspace]] feature "[[What's The Story?]]"<ref name="DB">{{DB|character|narhida|Hida, Nar}}</ref> in an entry published on [[September 28]], [[2006]].<ref name="DBDate">{{SWArchive|url=databank/updates/news20060928.html|text=What's the Story, Round 7}}</ref>

